      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t abort on fsal_fd_total_counter going negative. Since this total is reporting-only. LogCrit is enough.\n\nAlso, the check matches fsal_fd_global_counter, but that abort exists because a corrupt global count breaks LRU reclaim. Killing nfsd for a stats counter not sure if this is acceptable.\n\nToday only the global counter aborts on negative. STATE/TEMP mismatches do not. After this patch, those mismatches decrement total and crash the server.\n\nThat is worse with the parent change (1246797): close_fsal_fd() now calls remove_fd_lru() for STATE/TEMP with no \"already removed\" guard like the glist_null() check used for GLOBAL. A second close on a STATE/TEMP fd will drive this counter negative and abort.",
      "revId": "5a416e7aed8f3f6998c6aadaf2ca960b5fce4b91",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
